849c" :question/math-academy-id "q-8506" :question/problem "A point $P$ has Cartesian coordinates $(-8,-15).$ What are the polar coordinates of $P?$ Round your answer to two decimal places where necessary." :question/worked-solution "First, we determine $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-8)^{2}+(-15)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{64+225} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{289} \\\\  & =17\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the reference angle, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\theta }_{R} & =|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{-15}{-8})| \\\\  & ≈1.080\\,84.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the point $P$ lies in the third quadrant, we add the reference angle to $\\pi ,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta  & =\\pi +{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi +1.080\\,84 \\\\  & ≈4.22,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places. Therefore, the polar coordinates of $P$ are  $(17,4.22).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-8506/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b04084c-8e69-5f53-a95d-664aba54aec9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-8506"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-16947/selection/7b824242ecc65879f356d40d0d640569064f1f773fbf99405fa3d602170fffd9" :answer/id #uuid "bccce791-a7c6-5b4a-a101-356ddc500505" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(25,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-16947/selection/ba1b6931d252bd6ad3d981dda2961a354b5f20b73d1e92201b84bb245e1b0bf9" :answer/id #uuid "d2608e10-8363-5765-b03d-5c092d354dae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(5,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-16947/selection/ca63a72ddd5fea60f7fcab7c279dd88ac4415bb5fb1826f95ec2f9d1d560d57d" :answer/id #uuid "ddce594b-28ba-5396-89a7-d685dceb52b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1,\\frac{\\pi }{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-16947/selection/5befddedb48c635a645a02efdc5a9efcb78c94